  "id": "COMPOUND:31405 - PROTEIN:4983",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Alstoyunine H and Jurkat through a series of molecular interactions. Alstoyunine H is identified as a target of two distinct compounds, both of which are implicated in targeting Jurkat cells. The first compound, (4aR,8aS)-4a,7,7-trimethyl-3,4,5,6,8,8a-hexahydro-1H-naphthalen-2-one, is known to target Jurkat, and both Alstoyunine H and endothelial lipase are targets of this compound. The second compound, 1-[(2S,3S)-2-(3-Hydroxyprop-1-En-2-Yl)-3-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-Trihydroxy-6-(Hydroxymethyl)Oxan-2-Yl]Oxy-2,3-Dihydro-1-Benzofuran-5-Yl]Ethanone, also targets Jurkat, and Alstoyunine H is a target of this compound as well. These findings suggest that Alstoyunine H may play a role in the biological activity of these compounds, potentially influencing Jurkat cell function. The evidence is consistent with a pathway where Alstoyunine H acts as a target of compounds that interact with Jurkat, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
